-- SUM-TYPE-FIELDS-SPEC §3 S2: a field read from a value that could still be a
-- constructor which does not declare it is refused at CHECK time. Before this
-- rule every read below type-checked clean and died at run time, with a
-- message about a CONSIDER the drafter never wrote (§1.1).
--
-- The positive side — the same reads, narrowed so that they are legal — is
-- `ok/sum-fields/narrowing.l4`.
--
-- This file is also the acceptance test for §3 S4's DIAGNOSTIC requirement,
-- which is stricter than "report the missing field": §3.2 makes the message
-- explain the NARROWING, and says a rule for which that sentence cannot be
-- written is too clever and is cut. So there is one site here per shape of
-- explanation the renderer can produce, and the golden is where you read them.

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF
    Landlord HAS deposit      IS A NUMBER
    Tenant   HAS monthly_rent IS A NUMBER

DECLARE Wrapper
    HAS inner IS AN Actor

-- 1. NOT NARROWED AT ALL. A GIVEN parameter stands at the whole type; nothing
--    in a one-line body narrows it.
GIVEN a IS AN Actor
GIVETH A NUMBER
`plain` a MEANS a's monthly_rent

-- 2. THE RESIDUAL, and the sub-rule §3.2 says has to carry the teaching load.
--    `WHEN Tenant 1500` matches only SOME `Tenant`s, so it does not consume
--    the constructor and a `Tenant` still reaches the OTHERWISE. The message
--    must name that branch: the difference between this and a green program is
--    a property of a sub-pattern three lines above the error.
GIVEN a IS AN Actor
GIVETH A NUMBER
`refutable residual` a MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN Tenant 1500 THEN 1
    OTHERWISE a's deposit

-- 3. NARROWED TO THE WRONG ARM by a `WHEN`. `Landlord` is a constructor of
--    `Actor` and it simply has no `monthly_rent`; "narrow it first" would be
--    no advice at all here.
GIVEN a IS AN Actor
GIVETH A NUMBER
`wrong arm` a MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN Landlord d THEN a's monthly_rent
    OTHERWISE 0

-- 4. A BASE THAT IS NOT A NAME. `w's inner` is a projection, so there is no
--    binder for any branch to narrow, and the repair is to give it a name or
--    to match the payload — not to wrap it in a CONSIDER and keep projecting,
--    which would be refused again.
GIVEN w IS A Wrapper
GIVETH A NUMBER
`chained` w MEANS w's inner's monthly_rent

-- 5. A VALUE WRITTEN AS A CONSTRUCTOR. Already as narrow as it will ever get,
--    so the read is wrong about which constructor it is reading from.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`constructed` MEANS (Landlord OF 4000)'s monthly_rent

-- 6. THE SELECTOR AS A VALUE, with no base at all. §3 S2's second ruling:
--    `Proj` lowers to plain application, so a bare partial selector is the
--    same partial function and died the same way. (`apply` is written out
--    rather than imported so this file needs no prelude and its golden
--    carries no import-resolution log.)
GIVEN f IS A FUNCTION FROM Actor TO NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`apply` f MEANS f (Landlord OF 4000)

GIVETH A NUMBER
`as a value` MEANS `apply` monthly_rent

-- 7. EVERY CONSTRUCTOR ALREADY TAKEN. The arms above consume `Landlord` AND
--    `Tenant`, so the residual is empty — and an empty clamp would certify
--    every read under it, so the clamp is widened back to the whole type. That
--    widening is sound: nothing reaches this read at all. But it is not
--    "nothing narrowed this", which is what the message said before
--    `NarrowedByExhaustedBranches` existed — an explanation that is
--    affirmatively wrong about what happened, which is the one thing §3.2
--    rules out. Read the golden: the message says the arms took everything,
--    and the repair is to delete the arm rather than to narrow anything.
GIVEN a IS AN Actor
GIVETH A NUMBER
`exhausted` a MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN Landlord d THEN 0
    WHEN Tenant   r THEN 1
    OTHERWISE a's monthly_rent

-- 8. NARROWED TO THE WRONG ARM BY A QUANTIFIER. `EVERY Landlord a` is the
--    narrowing constructor of §0 — it says the rule ranges over landlords —
--    and it narrows `a` just as surely as a `WHEN` does, only to an arm that
--    does not declare the field. Distinct from case 3 because the drafter
--    wrote no `CONSIDER`: a message about "the branch above" would send them
--    looking for one. This is the only site in the tree that pins
--    `NarrowedByCast`, and §4 records that the quantifier-narrowed projection
--    has no other coverage anywhere.
DECLARE Action IS ONE OF
    Sign HAS signer IS AN Actor

GIVEN everyone IS A LIST OF Actor
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`quantified at the wrong arm` everyone MEANS
    EVERY Landlord a IN everyone
        WHO    a's monthly_rent AT LEAST 1000
        MUST   Sign (EXACTLY a)
        WITHIN 14
